ATRIX-test:unit:loan-mapped-movement-capture-repair]`). Repeated movement in both formats checks current ancestry while preserving historical reads after retirement (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-mapped-movement-current-lineage]`). The combined instance/sample/branch native product and its compacted selection preserve sample-specific membership, original holes and all three channels (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-mapped-movement-combined-products-and-compaction]`); this structural test grants no LC branch theorem. Every ancestor retains the child's binary format. Binary32 continuations admit square, movement and projected unary origins; ordinary reciprocal, ordinary root and binary arithmetic origins retain their binary64 restriction.

**Rule (Mapped Square continuation)** · `rule:nrz:matrix-loans-mapped-square`

The opt-in Square continuation admits current published center/total/error inputs in either native format. Materialized gathers and repeated product cells retain their exact immediate occupation, original map and current ancestor checks under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-mapped-movement`). The ordinary host-only Square route still refuses application origins. Fresh output declarations use the immediate source axis and extent; captured demand may retire after admission. Existing Square invocation, reservation and traversal inventories remain unchanged. Literal f64 endpoint squares at exactly represented small magnitudes check copied total-bound containment in both formats (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-mapped-square-gathered-both-formats]`), including repeated product incidence and an outside original reader (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-mapped-square-product-and-outside-reader]`). This continuation retains Square's existing per-step numerical-error interpretation; complete whole-expression numerical-error propagation remains an LC kernel obligation, and direct projected Square inputs follow (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-projected-square`).

**Rule (Direct projected unary consumers)** · `rule:nrz:matrix-loans-projected-square`

A checked projected unary operation retains its original input shape, independently checked output descriptor for Square, reciprocal or square root and native cell map. Admission authenticates the same original, product or gathered correspondence as movement and requires complete center/total/error source bundles in either format. Only `request_projected_elementwise` admits these projected recipes; ordinary and chained Square, reciprocal and square-root entry points refuse them before numerical allocation (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-projected-unary-entry-refusals]`). Source and destination must have identical coverage; both mismatch directions refuse with zero reads and return the repairable request (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-projected-coverage-mismatch]`). Both `RepresentedInputs` and `DeclaredBounds` are admitted: the latter retains the caller-declared component bounds as assumptions, and the kernel encloses the entire center/total box without certifying physical-input provenance (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-projected-unary-declared-bounds]`). A source with a bound but no error channel is refused. Projected unary arithmetic does not carry statistics until a projected Jacobian is implemented. The result uses the target axis and common application lifecycle. Bind companion owners once per tile, scan selected mask words, resolve one source cell per selected target cell and load only Center and Total per component. No intermediate copied tile or per-load reader Work phase is created. Error has `LocalOperation` scope under (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-error-scope`). Existing current-lineage checks govern application inputs and later continuations. `DeclaredBounds` projected results are terminal under the current-lineage `RepresentedInputs` requirement (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-projected-declared-bounds-terminal]`). Independent literal input intervals and exact local errors in both formats are (`[MATRIX-test:unit:loan-projected-square-native-consumers]`). Two selected two-component ce