**Decision (Retained prepared expm1 authority owner)** · `dec:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-owner`

Introduce one immutable matrix owner for the binary64 `enclosure.expm1-horner@1` law, together with its charged retaining uses. This is a prerequisite ownership slice beside (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-pointwise-slice`); it performs preparation and scalar reuse but admits no masked prepared application. Choose ownership of the producing CAS over propagating a graph borrow through `Heap`, the loan registry, every detached core, bundle and pin. Propagation is sound but would couple unrelated numerical owners and heap operations to one external graph lifetime, while still requiring all the same retention and accounting checks. A privately owned frozen graph gives the lifetime-free owner graph its actual authority, following (`dec:nrz:transcendental-scalar-owner`), (`[MATRIX-dec:matrix:prepared-expm1-owner]`). Keeping a borrowed plan beside the initial result facade, leaking a graph or replacing authority with a historical copy does not meet this decision.

