**Definition (Owned preparation and frozen law surface)** · `def:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-owner-surface`

The public constructor is `Heap::prepare_retained_expm1`: it consumes one uniquely owned `Cas`, borrows the original `Request`, and takes the represented domain `[f64; 2]`, preparation `Policy`, `ArithmeticContext`, `Counts` and the original mutable `ExecutionAccount`. Success returns a non-cloneable `RetainedExpm1` use; refusal returns the consumed CAS with the typed cause and no exposed law owner. Prior exact Work remains spent. A successful CAS preparation followed by lowering or physical-admission refusal may leave its checked lemma in the returned graph; this route promises no rollback beyond the CAS operation's own transaction. It accepts neither an existing `PreparedExpm1` nor a supplied `Prepared`, program, proof, key, coefficient array, reading or mutable/shared graph wrapper as admission authority.

Privately, one `Rc<PreparedExpm1Owner>` owns the moved `Cas`, the actual `Box<Prepared>` obtained by its own preparation, one inline `Expm1Program`, the admitted represented domain's endpoint bits, a sealed runtime `LawIdentity`, and its inventory/token/cleanup record. The program's fixed 128-coefficient array is inside that owner, not another allocation. The complete original request, context, coordinate association, exact domain, target and checked proof remain in the returned authority. A private immutable seal binds that authority and program to the represented domain, law/schedule/lowering and arithmetic revisions. Its identity is heap scope, original account and a fresh nonwrapping owner identity, independent of statement content. A use owns a separate `Rc<PreparedExpm1UseRecord>` containing its unique use identity, that exact owner edge, token and prepaid release entitlement. Neither private `Rc` nor a weak upgrade is exposed.

`RetainedExpm1::evaluate` borrows the use and returns the existing borrowed `Expm1Evaluation` or lossless `Expm1Failure`; the result cannot outlive the use through which it was obtained. Immutable authority/domain inspection is allowed. The native method calls the admitted scalar program without allocating, accessing CAS, replaying evidence or charging exact Work, preserving (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:prepared-expm1-native]`). Reading extraction remains data only. `Heap::retain_retained_expm1` authenticates a live use on its original account and returns a separately funded use or a typed refusal without changing the original. `Heap::release_retained_expm1` consumes one use through prepaid release, returning that same use on authentication refusal; ordinary drop has the same ownership effect. A charged inventory accessor reports that owner's unique inventory and individual uses without acquiring another use. No bare locator can construct or reacquire a use.

**Rule (Prepare, pair and freeze without self-reference)** · `rule:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-owner-freeze`

Preparation must call `Cas::prepare_expm1` itself, take its returned authority and perform the same represented-domain correspondence, checked coefficient import and outward export-parameter lowering as `PreparedExpm1::new`. Share these operations through a private owned-parts helper in the preparation module: it returns owned authority/program parts after its temporary mutable graph borrow ends. Move those parts and that same CAS into the immutable owner; do not store a borrowed `PreparedExpm1` beside its referent. The helper is no public `from_parts` or CAS authentication interface. After all fallible checks, inventory admission and private shell allocation, install the sealed owner and initial use together with their debits; no partially paired use escapes. This preserves the theorem and import/export premises of (`[CAS-thm:cas:enclosure-expm1-horner]`), (`[CAS-rule:cas:prepared-expm1-export]`).

