A numerical source pin and a law use have different last uses. Releasing the source after successful publication cannot release the result's law. Repair retains both while either can still be needed. Cancellation and abandonment release the detached law use after the last possible evaluation or evidence read and before the core's final liveness witness expires. A bundle retains its law until the bundle itself is destroyed: result pins, the published registry root and required delivery obligations can each delay that event. With no external law use, the last bundle's destruction can destroy the law owner; with an independent use still alive it cannot. Retiring one of several bundles never clears their shared owner's debit. No engine last-use scheduler is added.

