Preparation and lowering use the original account's cumulative ledger, preserve the existing exact tariffs and remain outside native evaluation. Their graph reservation is CAS-owned through `Cas::with_retained_graph`, not a caller estimate or managed token (`[CAS-rule:cas:retained-graph-scope]`). Consuming a pre-existing CAS moves its already allocated graph; freeze performs no graph clone or additional graph-sized allocation. Its original construction and any preparation growth are paid in the existing CAS scopes by the caller. Retaining it for longer retains the whole graph, including unrelated judgments; no subgraph extraction or discount is implied. Moving that graph into the shared header adds the actual inline CAS/header storage to the new managed allowance. It does not turn logical `GraphCounts.payload_bytes` into a physical allocator census or install a new persistent CAS registration.

