The common residence inventory counts the owner allowance once by `LawIdentity`, every live or conservatively expired use separately, and vacant table capacity separately. Its prepared-owner observation distinguishes H, E, use headers/edges and the separately scoped retained graph; per-bundle observations identify their shared law rather than adding H+E for every bundle or pin. A live law or unreconciled prepared debit prevents `Residence::Empty` even with zero destination elements. Extend both the byte traversal and the occupied predicate in `loan/scans.rs`; adding bytes to `resource_bytes` alone would miss this case. Scope exceptions stay visible rather than being advertised as a complete physical graph measurement, preserving (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-residence`).

