## Closed kernel families for masked application · `sec:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-families`

**Decision (One application mechanism with closed family members)** · `dec:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family`

Extract the member contract of the Square and retained expm1 applications in (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-pointwise-slice`), (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-prepared-expm1-slice`), and admit binary64 reciprocal through that contract. Preserve the two existing public entry points, accepted inputs, typed refusals and their ordering, numerical results, authority identities, Work and byte pins, and every ownership transition. Their existing controls must pass unchanged. The additional entry point is `Heap::request_pointwise_reciprocal(PointwiseRequest<f64>, account)`, returning the existing `ApplicationRequest<f64>` and using the same evaluate, publish, cancel and reader interfaces. The Square entry point remains Square-only, including its reciprocal refusal. This specifies one code slice; it adds no executable support or changed tests or pins in this documentation decision.

Choose the existing `Recipe::Elementwise(Elementwise::Reciprocal)` law, not `Recipe::PositiveReciprocal`. The former already supplies a checked descriptor power, a whole-box native enclosure and the allocation-free `kernels/nonlinear.rs::evaluate_selected` seam used by Square. It supports either sign when the complete outward divisor box excludes zero. A box containing zero has a typed cell refusal; this slice does not split its domain or resolve an LC sign barrier. The positive-reciprocal map in `kernels/reciprocal.rs` instead imports rational references, coefficients and offsets, allocates intermediate images and contracts an affine map over ordered inputs. Lifting that schedule would require a coefficient prelude and different inventories. The selected unary member needs neither. Its native and scalar premises are (`[MATRIX-test:integration:native-reciprocal-encloses-exact-rational-endpoints]`), (`[SCALAR-sec:scalar:guarantees]`), (`[SCALAR-test:integration:binary64-primitive-boundary-oracle]`). This addresses one kernel needed by (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-kernel-interface`), not the physical LC composition in (`req:nrz:lc-evaluation-matrix-owner`).

Exp is a valid separate candidate, but is larger here: `PreparedExp` borrows its producing graph and composes an authenticated expm1 basis with checked addition of one and an absolute endpoint test. Managed exp would need its own retained composition/correspondence and lossless `ExpFailure` representation, including `TargetNotCertifiable`, under (`[MATRIX-def:matrix:prepared-exp-outcomes]`), (`[MATRIX-rule:matrix:prepared-exp-evidence]`), (`[SCALAR-rule:scalar:prepared-exp-composition]`). Reciprocal already has the required native form and fits the existing three-reading storage and outcome widths. No new CAS theorem, retained owner kind, endpoint conversion or source-provenance mechanism is needed for this choice.

**Rule (Private closed member contract)** · `rule:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-contract`

Use a private closed enum with Square, retained prepared expm1, reciprocal and positive square root members, extended only by the ordered Product and Quotient profiles in (`dec:nrz:matrix-loans-binary-members`). It is a borrowed, validated view of the existing checked operation and optional prepared correspondence/attachment, constructed at the existing authentication boundaries; it is not another stored authority, allocation or debit. The original `Recipe` identity, original operation, structural-exclusion witnesses and optional prepared binding remain the persistent seal in the existing core and bundle. Keep their layouts and existing cancellation inventories unchanged; the bounded binary inventory extension is specified in (`rule:nrz:matrix-loans-binary-resources`). An enum match supplies the finite member operations; there is no public trait implementation, plugin registry, callback, generic cache, coefficient/program constructor or caller-supplied authority. Do not replace one `prepared.is_some()` switch with a permissive “all other elementwise laws” branch. Reconstructing the view must reject an unknown or inconsistent combination before using its profile.

Each member supplies its original-operation admission and exact identity comparison; closed numerical law or retained current authority and lowering revisions; admissible precision, coverage and input representation; mathematical and represented domains; target kind; output reading/endpoint semantics; unchanged whole-shape and separately checked per-cell invocation allowance; lossless numerical outcomes; and its fixed allocation, visit and retention profile. These are one indivisible selection, never independently caller-selectable fields. “Exact enclosure” below means containment of the exact function over the represented input set with no requested relative or absolute tolerance; it does not mean an exactly represented center or a zero radius. Relative and absolute targets must identify the quantity and representation they bound. There is no admitted absolute-target member in this slice, and no default target for a later member.

