Keep all Square, retained-owner, expm1, reciprocal and square-root controls unchanged, including their public refusals, literal Work/byte pins, formats, cleanup and heap-drop behavior under (`req:nrz:matrix-loans-kernel-family-controls`), (`req:nrz:matrix-loans-square-root-controls`). Add public product and quotient lifecycles using independently decoded exact rationals for centers, radii and all four rectangle corners. Independently round the exact rational product or quotient of the decoded operand centers to the admitted native format nearest, ties to even, and compare the stored center bits; equivalently prove the exact adjacent-midpoint inequalities with equality allowed only for even significand parity. Cover both signs, canonical positive zero including rounded zero, midpoint ties with both parity outcomes, and the fixed `2^-149` or `2^-1074` subnormal quantum for its format. A platform multiply or divide or another production invocation is only a regression comparison. Reject an adjacent wrong center even when recomputed error and total still enclose the images. Separately check nominal error and total around the actual stored center with exact dyadic arithmetic: require the exact nominal product or quotient in `[y-e,y+e]`, the exact four-corner image hull in `[y-R,y+R]`, and finite nonnegative `e<=R`. For a separated divisor, exact rational endpoint quotients and their hull are the oracle; multiplying production reciprocal/enclosure outputs is not independent evidence. These independent test obligations add no runtime certificate or native Work. Include irrational-free but nonrepresentable products/quotients, mixed signs, negative divisors, signed zeros, unit identities, underflow, adjacent subnormals, normal/subnormal transitions, huge balanced ratios, overflowing outward neighbours and box/displacement overflow. Exercise exact and outward-only contact with zero, zero numerators with invalid divisors, and a direct quotient whose reciprocal-first evaluation